        "id": 129557,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-28T03:58:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had a big one because I had big maps, so it had a 4 inch diameter inside, I fit about 10 maps in that one without them getting rolled too tight. &nbsp;If they weren't as thick (mine were Really heavy) I could probably have done 25. &nbsp;I would lay them flat and roll them together as one roll.</p><p>If they are shipped rolled they will probably come in a container that will work for storage.</p><p>The bad thing about rolled maps is you want to have nice weights for the corners, which is good for paper maps anyway, whether they curl or slide.</p>",
